                          "emptyText": "No uptime history yet. Each agent writes one row per day, so the first appears after a day of running."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "incidents",
                  "label": "Incidents",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "type": "conditional",
                      "when": {
                        "source": {
                          "kind": "stream",
                          "event": "ui",
                          "path": "hintsOn"
                        },
                        "op": "eq",
                        "value": true
                      },
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "type": "note",
                          "title": "What is recorded",
                          "lines": [
                            "link_down and link_up - the machine lost or regained its internet connection.",
                            "ip_changed - its public address moved, which matters because most of these services tie an account to an address.",
                            "latency_spike - one episode of unusually high latency, with its peak and how long it lasted. One row per episode, not one per slow second.",
                            "unit_down and unit_crash - a service stopped, and whether it exited cleanly or not.",
                            "agent_gap - the agent itself was not running. That time is excluded from uptime rather than counted as good."
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
